{
  "dom_id": "step-q339829",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2x+8)}{2-x}=$\n\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The function $\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2x+8)}{2-x}$ is well defined for $x>-4,$ and $x\\ne 2$ and so to find this limit we substitute $x=1$ into the above expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2x+8)}{2-x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2(1)+8)}{2-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(10)}{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{log}⁡({10}^{1}) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
